---
title: Creamy Pancetta Pasta Del Maresciallo
description: An easy, quick Southern Italian pasta tossed in a creamy tomato and pancetta sauce.
course: main
cuisine: Italian
servings: 4
time required: 35 minutes
prep time: 10 minutes
cook time: 25 minutes
source: https://www.the-pasta-project.com/creamy-pancetta-pasta-del-maresciallo/
image: https://www.the-pasta-project.com/wp-content/uploads/Creamy-Pancetta-Pasta-del-Maresciallo.-6.jpg
tags:
  - pasta
  - italian
  - pancetta
  - creamy
  - quick
---

Cube the @pancetta{200%g} if needed, then peel and finely chop the @onion{1}.

Heat the @extra virgin olive oil{3-4%tbsp} in a #large skillet{}. Cook the onion for a couple of minutes until soft, then add the pancetta and sauté until it starts to brown.

Add the @tomato passata{400%g} with a pinch of @salt and @black pepper. Cook over high heat for ~{5%minutes}, then simmer gently on low heat for another ~{10%minutes}. Stir in the @fresh cream{200%ml} and cook a further ~{5%minutes}.

Meanwhile, bring a #large pot{} of water to a boil. Salt it once boiling, then cook the @penne pasta{400%g} until al dente per the package instructions.

Drain the pasta, add it to the sauce, mix, and sauté over high heat for ~{2-3%minutes}. Serve immediately topped with grated @Parmigiano Reggiano{50%g} and chopped @parsley.
